<!-- ============================ ENGLISH ============================ -->
<section class="version" id="en" lang="en">
<h1>Privacy Policy — Treino CGU</h1>
<p class="meta">Effective 5 October 2026 · Version 1.0. The Portuguese version above prevails in case of conflict.</p>

<div class="summary">
  <ul>
    <li>The app works fully offline and <strong>has no internet permission</strong>.</li>
    <li>There is no sign-up, login, advertising, analytics, tracking, or third-party library that collects data.</li>
    <li>Your progress and favorites stay <strong>on your device only</strong>. We do not receive, see, or store them.</li>
  </ul>
</div>

<h2>1. Who is responsible</h2>
<p>The <strong>Treino CGU</strong> app (Google Play ID: <code>com.kora.treinocgu</code>) is developed and published by <strong>Kora</strong>, an independent developer (“we”). For the purposes of Brazil’s General Data Protection Law (Lei nº 13.709/2018, “LGPD”), Kora is the controller of any personal data processed as described in this policy.</p>
<p>Privacy contact: <a href="mailto:edbogosian@investmaestri.com">edbogosian@investmaestri.com</a></p>

<h2>2. Data the app does not collect</h2>
<p>The app does not request, read, or send your name, email, phone number, documents, contacts, location, photos, camera, microphone, files, advertising ID, device identifiers, or any other personal information. The app requests no sensitive Android permissions.</p>

<h2>3. Data stored on your device only</h2>
<p>To show your progress, the app saves the following in its private Android storage:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Per section test:</strong> number of attempts, best score, last score, number of error-free attempts, and the date and time of the last attempt.</li>
  <li><strong>Per submitted mock exam:</strong> date and time, chosen size (100%, 50%, or 25%), total items, correct, wrong, and blank items, time used, time limit, and whether time ran out. Only the most recent mock exams are kept.</li>
  <li><strong>Favorites:</strong> the list of items you marked with the star.</li>
  <li><strong>Study indicators:</strong> the total number of questions answered and the study dates used to calculate your day streak and best streak.</li>
  <li><strong>During a mock exam in progress:</strong> selected answers, items flagged for review, and elapsed time, so the exam is not lost if Android closes the app in the background.</li>
</ul>
<p>This data contains no name, email, or text you type, and it is not sent to us or to anyone else. Android’s app sandbox prevents other apps from reading it.</p>

<h2>4. Android backup</h2>
<p>If backup is turned on in your device settings, Android may include the data in section 3 in your Google Account backup and restore it when you install the app on another device. Google operates this service under the <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy?hl=en">Google Privacy Policy</a>; we have no access to these backups. On Android 9 or later, the backup is end-to-end encrypted with your device’s screen-lock PIN, pattern, or password. You can turn backup off in Android settings.</p>

<h2>5. Google Play</h2>
<p>The app is downloaded and updated through Google Play, which processes data under Google’s privacy policy. Google Play Console shows us aggregate statistics (for example, install and rating counts) and technical crash and freeze reports from users who chose to share diagnostic data with Google. We use this information only to measure the app’s reach and fix bugs, and we do not combine it with other data to identify anyone. Public reviews you post on Google Play are visible to us and may receive a public reply.</p>

<h2>6. Contacting us by email</h2>
<p>If you write to us, we receive your email address and the content of your message. We use them only to reply and handle your request. The legal bases are legitimate interest (LGPD art. 7, IX) and, for data-subject requests, compliance with a legal obligation (art. 7, II). The mailbox is hosted by an email provider acting as a processor. We keep the conversation only as long as needed for that purpose and delete it on request, unless the law requires us to keep it.</p>

<h2>7. Sharing</h2>
<p>We do not sell, share, or transfer personal data to third parties. The app makes no international data transfers.</p>

<h2>8. Security</h2>
<p>Because the app transmits no data, there is no network traffic to protect. Local data stays in the app’s private storage, protected by Android’s sandbox and permission system. Email is kept in an account that only the developer can access. We recommend keeping your device’s screen lock turned on.</p>

<h2>9. Retention and deletion</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>On-device data:</strong> kept until you delete it. You can clear the app’s data in <em>Settings › Apps › Treino CGU › Storage</em> or uninstall the app. Menu names vary by manufacturer.</li>
  <li><strong>Google Account backup:</strong> can be managed or deleted in Android and Google Account backup settings.</li>
  <li><strong>Email:</strong> deleted when no longer needed or on request.</li>
</ul>
<p>Because the app has no user accounts and no server, we hold no app data that could be deleted on our side.</p>

<h2>10. Your rights</h2>
<p>Under LGPD art. 18, you can ask us, by email, for confirmation that processing exists; access; correction; anonymization, blocking, or deletion; portability; information about sharing; and information about withholding consent and withdrawal of consent. We will reply within 15 days (art. 19, II). You may also file a petition with Brazil’s <a href="https://www.gov.br/anpd/pt-br">National Data Protection Authority (ANPD)</a>.</p>
<p>As a small-scale processing agent (ANPD Resolution CD/ANPD nº 2/2022, art. 11), we have not appointed a data protection officer. The communication channel for data subjects is the email in section 1.</p>

<h2>11. Children and teenagers</h2>
<p>The app is intended for people aged 18 or older who are studying for Brazilian civil-service exams that require a university degree. The app collects no data from any user, including children and teenagers. If a parent or guardian believes a minor has emailed us personal data, they can ask us to delete it using the contact above.</p>

<h2>12. Independence</h2>
<p>Treino CGU is an independent study tool. It is not affiliated with the Controladoria-Geral da União (CGU), Cebraspe, or FGV, and it does not represent any government body.</p>

<h2>13. Changes to this policy</h2>
<p>If this policy changes, we will publish the new version at this same address with a new effective date. If the app ever starts collecting data, this policy and the Google Play Data safety section will be updated before the change takes effect.</p>
